# Who owns which part of the schedule.
#
# Honest about what this does: everyone listed here can push straight to main, so in normal use
# nothing here is enforced and no review is requested. It earns its place in one case -- if
# somebody without push access opens a pull request, GitHub asks the right person to look at it
# instead of defaulting to the repository owner.
#
# It is also the shortest answer to "whose is this row?", which is why the same names appear in
# each track file's own header.

/tracks/accounting.md   @AJ-Technext
/tracks/pms.md          @phillip-technext
/tracks/trackc.md       @jett-technext
/tracks/unified.md      @jett-technext
/tracks/joint_walk.md   @jett-technext

# Shared reference tables -- changing these affects every track, so they are deliberately not
# owned by one track's owner.
/roster.md              @jett-technext
/week.md                @jett-technext

# The build and its configuration.
/build.py               @jett-technext
/page.template.html     @jett-technext
/baseline-clashes.json  @jett-technext
/.github/               @jett-technext
